WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:07.400
Americans need to pay attention to the

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.350
civil war inside of Yemen because its

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:11.060
development has ramifications for

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.670
American national security interests. The

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:15.380
country is home to al Qaeda in the

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.480
Arabian Peninsula, one of al Qaeda's most

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.730
virulent affiliates. It has attacked the

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:21.380
United States over three times since its

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.349
founding in 2009, and there is also a small

00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:27.259
ISIS presence. But more importantly, today,

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:30.109
is the way that Yemen has affected our

00:00:30.109 --> 00:00:32.630
Gulf partners. Saudi Arabia is now

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.760
embroiled in the war in Yemen. Saudi

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.760
Arabia cannot risk having a destabilized

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:38.809
Yemeni state on its southern

00:00:38.809 --> 00:00:40.910
border, and it will continue to distract the

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.890
country, even as the United States asks the

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.289
Saudi's to step up increasingly inside

00:00:45.289 --> 00:00:47.390
of Syria. It's not just the Saudis who are

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.609
involved in Yemen. The Emiratis have also

00:00:49.609 --> 00:00:51.679
deployed a significant task force inside

00:00:51.679 --> 00:00:52.820
of the country to assist in

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:54.949
counterterrorism operations. The

00:00:54.949 --> 00:00:56.960
deployment inside of Yemen means that

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.940
our Gulf Arab partners do not have the

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.159
military to support our efforts inside

00:01:01.159 --> 00:01:03.469
of Syria, and therefore the United States

00:01:03.469 --> 00:01:05.150
needs to care about what is going on in

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:06.850
the war in Yemen.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:12.640
Should the U.S. support its regional partners in Yemen? If so, how?

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.090
Let us know in the comments section, and

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:15.530
let us know what other topics you want

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:22.630
AEI scholars to cover in 60 seconds.

